/* Gamestage fonts, arcade theme.

   Arcade uses the same two faces as the base pairing, DM Sans and Unbounded.
   It named Bungee as its display face until GSUI-171, which is a face the
   design never names.

   The two declarations are repeated here and the two files are not. The
   `fonts-arcade` item depends on `@gamestage/fonts`, which is what ships
   gamestage-fonts/, so a customer installing the arcade theme gets one copy of
   each face on disk, about 88KB, rather than two. If arcade ever takes a face
   the base pairing does not have, add its @font-face here and its file beside
   the others; do not duplicate a face that is already shared.

   A theme may name any family it likes, because type.fontFamily.interface and
   .display are tokens; what it cannot do is load one. Without this stylesheet
   the family is simply absent and the theme looks as though it changed nothing.

   Import once at the root, before gamestage-tokens.css, in place of
   gamestage-fonts.css. Nothing here reaches a third-party origin; the reason,
   the licences and the provenance are in gamestage-fonts/README.md (GSUI-149).
   The url() paths are relative to this stylesheet and resolve the same way in
   this repository and in a customer's app. */

@font-face {
  font-family: 'DM Sans';
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 400 900;
  font-display: swap;
  src: url('./gamestage-fonts/dm-sans-latin.woff2') format('woff2');
  unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA,
    U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193,
    U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;
}

@font-face {
  font-family: 'Unbounded';
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 500 900;
  font-display: swap;
  src: url('./gamestage-fonts/unbounded-latin.woff2') format('woff2');
  unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA,
    U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193,
    U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;
}
